From 5779c33aa1fc7e95bd1089ccea54f571ab953671 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 09:45:31 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 01/10] Write the per-point exports by blocks of points, in
 parallel processes

Each exporter selected one point at a time from the lazy zarr store and read
every variable separately: about 11 Dask reads per point, each decompressing
the whole 10-point chunk again, before formatting the file. For 500 points
over one hourly year, to_fsm took 50 s and to_cryogrid 47 s.

topo_export.export_points() reads blocks of consecutive points aligned on
the chunks of the store once, then writes the file of each point; the blocks
are shared between n_jobs joblib loky processes, each reading its own blocks.
The per-point code of each format is unchanged (moved to module-level
_write_* functions), and the files are identical to before, byte for byte
for text formats, whatever the number of processes.

- to_fsm, to_TC, to_micromet_single_station, to_crocus, to_snowpack,
  to_geotop, to_cryogrid and the met files of to_fsm2oshd take n_jobs;
  the Topoclass wrappers pass project CPU_cores
- 500 points x 8760 h: to_fsm 50.4 s -> 24.8 s (1 process) -> 15.7 s (2),
  to_cryogrid 47.3 s -> 15.1 s -> 8.2 s
- to_crocus and to_micromet_single_station work again (undefined pt;
  to_crocus also took the max of string point names and renamed a
  dimension its point dataset does not have); CROCUS files hold their point
  on a Number_of_points dimension, as SURFEX reads them
- to_fsm2oshd creates its folder and rejects an unknown ds_tvt string
- one progress line per block instead of one line per file
- tests: same files with 1 and 2 processes for every exporter, values of
  the store in the FSM file, CROCUS layout, MicroMet ids and header

